  "notes": "{落胆|らくたん} expresses disappointment or discouragement, typically at a deeper level than casual disappointment.\n\nWORD FORMATION:\n{落|らく} (fall) + {胆|たん} (courage/spirit) — literally \"one's spirit falls\"\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜に{落胆|らくたん}する: to be disappointed by ~\n- {落胆|らくたん}を{隠|かく}せない: unable to hide disappointment\n- {落胆|らくたん}している{場合|ばあい}ではない: no time to be dejected\n\nREGISTER:\nMore formal and literary than がっかり. Common in news reports, written language, and formal speech.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- がっかり: disappointed (casual, everyday)\n- {失望|しつぼう}: disappointment (also formal)",
